   "note": "203 Skeledirge, Torcherto: \"This attack does 20 more damage for each Benched Pokemon (both yours and your opponent's).\" Re-measured 2026-07-30 against the committed native engine with per-seat bench control (Issue #213 / ADR-0083). Fits printed + 20 x (atkBench + defBench) exactly; attacker-axis slope 20 equals defender-axis slope 20, which is what NAMES the combined family per REQ-AUDIT-0019. The energy and hand axes are FLAT because both benches are pinned across them — that flatness is what makes hand size unfittable, and its absence is what let this attack ship an exact-looking atk_hand/5 fit. Rows transcribed from Issue #224's preserved table: reports/attack_audit/measurements.json no longer exists, so per-row hand size and energy count could not be recovered and are null.",
